##Internal Escalation Message
To: Project Manager, Technical Lead, QA Lead
Subject: Day 4 escalation – resource absence, POS critical defects and Taxi Booking risk

DEV-3 is unavailable for two working days and two tasks need confirmed cover. Proposed DEV-2/DEV-4 reassignment is subject to skill and capacity checks. Restaurant POS has 12 defects, including 3 critical, hold release until all critical defects are fixed and independently retested. Log the reporting feature as CR-01 and estimate it before approval. Taxi Booking is 30% complete against a 10-working-day plan, do not guarantee the original date without a critical-path review.

Decisions requested: approve cover and resequencing, confirm defect owners and release gate, assign CR-01 estimator, authorize Taxi Booking client-options discussion. Record decision owners and due dates.

Conclusion
Day 4 demonstrates controlled responses to resource disruption, scope change, quality defects and deadline pressure. Validate capacity before reallocating work, use formal change control, block release for critical defects, and communicate delivery options supported by evidence. All proposed estimates and owner assignments remain provisional until confirmed.
